 "sentences": [
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "text": "Every chat app you use sits on the same simple blueprint."
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "text": "It starts with one server running the code and the database together."
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "text": "For a thousand people chatting, that single machine is perfectly fine."
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "text": "Then a group chat goes viral, and the processor pins at one hundred percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "text": "So you add more servers and put a load balancer in front of them."
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "text": "It spreads every connection across the healthy servers."
  },
  {
   "id": "s7",
   "text": "Now every message still hits one database, and that becomes the bottleneck."
  },
  {
   "id": "s8",
   "text": "Recent messages move into a cache, so most reads come from memory."
  },
  {
   "id": "s9",
   "text": "Sending should feel instant, but push notifications, previews and search indexing are slow."
  },
  {
   "id": "s10",
   "text": "Should the sender wait for all of that?"
  },
  {
   "id": "s11",
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "id": "s12",
   "text": "A queue takes the slow jobs, and background workers finish them later."
  },
  {
   "id": "s13",
   "text": "The system is not a pile of trendy tools."
  },
  {
   "id": "s14",
   "text": "Every piece exists because a real bottleneck appeared."
  },
  {
   "id": "s15",
   "text": "Start simple, find the bottleneck, add the smallest fix, and repeat."
  }
 ],
